  "summary": "Malicious code in voxweaver (PyPI)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (864111ebda91af60c9791e2352b3d95b32e6b6da08e9bcb0a674a6a23ab3ffdd)\nAnalysis of voxweaver 0.1.0 on PyPI surfaced no indicators of installer-side harm. No install-time or import-time network activity, no credential or environment scraping, no filesystem persistence, no suspicious lifecycle hooks, and no evidence of silent relay, dropper, or backdoor behavior were observed in the package contents.\n\n## Source: kam193 (98de0e1f12e0c4b69583e08c1cd46876975b49c6803d93483c136ee2f6e62f68)\nThis campaign consists of similar loader packages, which provide executing code from a given URL. While they do not contain the malicious payload and the usage remains unknown, they are clearly a coordinated campaign to place multiple deceptive ways to load malicious code.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: MALICIOUS - The campaign has clearly malicious intent, like infostealers.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-10-voice-synthesis-profiles\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - other\n\n\n - Downloads and executes a remote malicious script.\n",
